 this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =1, & \\,{m}_{2} & =4, & \\,{m}_{3} & =3, & \\,{m}_{4} & =1, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-2, & \\,{x}_{2} & =-1, & \\,{x}_{3} & =3, & \\,{x}_{4} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-2-4+9+5 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $8\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163226/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7ea6678-6624-5853-b137-be255a3e694e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163226"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163251/selection/8677255573c89f51bbda2655bf0990b3a6ef52dd073a8086551da4668a68282d" :answer/id #uuid "5ce0541a-d385-5253-b477-69c14002512a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163251/selection/85288a6a013fc2ec3b8651470e5e8ff4e6d78cbb846c53a9af4e925ac132429e" :answer/id #uuid "0ae31a33-c76d-5796-b850-58baacaab227" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{41}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163251/selection/b747c7baf2e19c943c6944d2b53574bc01c8a73c27d3f4dc85d331929f4baae8" :answer/id #uuid "0274c3b5-fd65-565a-ad24-05a1b8797c91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{23}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163251/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer/id #uuid "e5801ff4-a13a-5e3e-8837-365cb96ece29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163251/selection/718ff1f1e9146b5d5d2cf798138ec0393245e544620d23b1f48534b92efd546a" :answer/id #uuid "7da8a0c7-7196-5d23-a15b-e020b560e69c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163251/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ae0f3cd-030f-5d79-a238-f3e185f59fcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163251/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer-field/choices ["q-163251/selection/8677255573c89f51bbda2655bf0990b3a6ef52dd073a8086551da4668a68282d" "q-163251/selection/85288a6a013fc2ec3b8651470e5e8ff4e6d78cbb846c53a9af4e925ac132429e" "q-163251/selection/b747c7baf2e19c943c6944d2b53574bc01c8a73c27d3f4dc85d331929f4baae8" "q-163251/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" "q-163251/selection/718ff1f1e9146b5d5d2cf798138ec0393245e544620d23b1f48534b92efd546a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163251" :question/id #uuid "d06c244a-0804-5d77-966b-56ff5941b06f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163251" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses ${m}_{1}=5\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{2}=1\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{3}=2\\,\\text{kg},$ and ${m}_{4}=4\\,\\text{kg}$ located at ${x}_{1}=1,$ ${x}_{2}=4,$ ${x}_{3}=0.5,$ and ${x}_{4}=1.5,$ respectively, along the $x$-axis, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =5, & \\,{m}_{2} & =1, & \\,{m}_{3} & =2, & \\,{m}_{4} & =4, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =4, & \\,{x}_{3} & =0.5, & \\,{x}_{4} & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3}+{m}_{4} \\\\  & =5+1+2+4 \\\\  & =12\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 0.5+4\\cdot 1.5 \\\\  & =5+4+1+6 \\\\  & =16\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{16}{12}=\\frac{4}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163251/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163251"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-163082"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/4561f2a4671ae67720e44d334d8bf75525fd72aeee62994cfea70c300702c5b4.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =2, & \\,{m}_{2} & =3, & \\,{m}_{3} & =1, & \\,{m}_{4} & =5, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =3, & \\,{x}_{3} & =5, & \\,{x}_{4} & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3}+{m}_{4} \\\\  & =2+3+1+5 \\\\  & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 5+5\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =2+9+5+30 \\\\  & =46.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{46}{11}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-163248/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "94495d0f-113a-5982-aaa1-889afd77323f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163248/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "79ea19ab-dcf8-5de1-b08a-31b9650a8720" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163248/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "5a7bbd08-d3fa-595e-800c-79534a9c74e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163248/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer/id #uuid "621c4f03-8fc0-572e-9cc6-a8edabb0138c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163248/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "627e027a-743c-5174-af84-24d7bb237d17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163248/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef0bb935-e8da-5c35-bd8d-f23b92bdbfa1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163248/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-163248/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-163248/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-163248/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-163248/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" "q-163248/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163248" :question/id #uuid "dea7cb11-e94a-5589-afd8-6a0286d30694" :question/math-academy-id "q-163248" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses ${m}_{1}=3\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{2}=6\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{3}=1\\,\\text{kg},$ and ${m}_{4}=5\\,\\text{kg}$ located at ${x}_{1}=-2,$ ${x}_{2}=2.5,$ ${x}_{3}=1,$ and ${x}_{4}=4,$ respectively, along the $x$-axis, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =3, & \\,{m}_{2} & =6, & \\,{m}_{3} & =1, & \\,{m}_{4} & =5, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-2, & \\,{x}_{2} & =2.5, & \\,{x}_{3} & =1, & \\,{x}_{4} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =3+6+1+5 \\\\  & =15\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-2)+6\\cdot 2.5+1\\cdot 1+5\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-6+15+1+20 \\\\  & =30\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{30}{15}=2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163248/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163248"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163262/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer/id #uuid "3e49df17-57f2-5eb8-ae44-fc6b8031dc3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163262/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "851cac12-982e-50e8-9788-2a000859bf91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163262/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "e426e25f-5cb7-55ad-afa7-0d3135f470c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163262/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "c0528160-b3d8-5036-b377-96668342dcc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163262/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "a7432724-7d27-5d01-9e02-ddf486aca1b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163262/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5546ee8d-9939-557b-92f3-5f610240f682" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163262/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer-field/choices ["q-163262/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" "q-163262/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-163262/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-163262/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-163262/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163262" :question/id #uuid "349a8392-b508-5af5-9c2a-95ec7cbe6f78" :question/math-academy-id "q-163262" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/dc16f02e1eb47605ae2f21c64fd0f5c2c2bde6526a22d3965da5fa991869524e.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =7, & \\,{m}_{2} & =4, & \\,{m}_{3} & =1, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =2, & \\,{x}_{3} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =7+4+1 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =7\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-7+8+3 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{4}{12}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163262/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163262"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163265/selection/774940da4ab3b26727b8db6c1c90fb931ece0a7759ec47b6581e5af495721ce1" :answer/id #uuid "282b76da-d8e5-55a5-aac5-973e0aa034ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163265/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "e834928b-0632-5d33-a77a-66fcb84f8168" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163265/selection/9abe4a199d76ee8b6a753464dca7eea17463a2db6cbd7e4173e6e9103279cdba" :answer/id #uuid "d814f6e4-08ab-5ece-a80f-c228e6aacee4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163265/selection/df817bb9da38e9cb484386a26fe6e5e9faf2ff1998e6e5a28c6ff4087baf96e1" :answer/id #uuid "17bf30f2-6a76-542e-85d7-e672149638de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163265/selection/4582dbd6025ba0c110f8e23964efc62e8612751348ffad003e8834a5780c1878" :answer/id #uuid "bc1968e9-44b7-59b3-9bd3-e1ac7131a921" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163265/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0de721e-dfcf-5791-941e-825cf03f9cc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163265/selection/774940da4ab3b26727b8db6c1c90fb931ece0a7759ec47b6581e5af495721ce1" :answer-field/choices ["q-163265/selection/774940da4ab3b26727b8db6c1c90fb931ece0a7759ec47b6581e5af495721ce1" "q-163265/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-163265/selection/9abe4a199d76ee8b6a753464dca7eea17463a2db6cbd7e4173e6e9103279cdba" "q-163265/selection/df817bb9da38e9cb484386a26fe6e5e9faf2ff1998e6e5a28c6ff4087baf96e1" "q-163265/selection/4582dbd6025ba0c110f8e23964efc62e8612751348ffad003e8834a5780c1878"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163265" :question/id #uuid "3b1a5ca7-9bfa-5080-b5aa-33e63e68a521" :question/math-academy-id "q-163265" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/e16f9309d74f81f419ed96e995750bcad21a2770f214c49ee537f22ca25aac2e.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =2, & \\,{m}_{2} & =3, & \\,{m}_{3} & =4, & \\,{m}_{4} & =5, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3, & \\,{x}_{2} & =-2, & \\,{x}_{3} & =-0.5, & \\,{x}_{4} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3}+{m}_{4} \\\\  & =2+3+4+5 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot (-0.5)+5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6-6-2+10 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{-4}{14}=-\\frac{2}{7}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163265/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163265"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163276/selection/718ff1f1e9146b5d5d2cf798138ec0393245e544620d23b1f48534b92efd546a" :answer/id #uuid "6a5685dc-1889-5ab3-8142-d0e7b22bea9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163276/selection/ed43d5224151224cedff9572a0bc31a320bd7a8ebd2aa526ca5884904c9d6cb4" :answer/id #uuid "bca38a90-8e59-5a46-9767-05b106807456" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163276/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" :answer/id #uuid "90ec524d-8311-5fab-8f18-9800880c2288" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163276/selection/1a9483841df301d0d8304986bfec9a52b4f49d31cfd2980ff1d8d6f175662caf" :answer/id #uuid "3147cbe1-f22f-5050-9d5d-2c0ace8a9135" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163276/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" :answer/id #uuid "da9faa1f-5cc9-591f-b3bb-705b2f9c1ceb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163276/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0c4040e3-8350-548f-9e5f-98b284791773" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163276/selection/718ff1f1e9146b5d5d2cf798138ec0393245e544620d23b1f48534b92efd546a" :answer-field/choices ["q-163276/selection/718ff1f1e9146b5d5d2cf798138ec0393245e544620d23b1f48534b92efd546a" "q-163276/selection/ed43d5224151224cedff9572a0bc31a320bd7a8ebd2aa526ca5884904c9d6cb4" "q-163276/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" "q-163276/selection/1a9483841df301d0d8304986bfec9a52b4f49d31cfd2980ff1d8d6f175662caf" "q-163276/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163276" :question/id #uuid "c900d2eb-6484-5d59-9646-3135c16323c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-163276" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/e55b3a19251f3470401c081b24a90e90674844ce47d617dffd68bf161e2b7199.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=2,\\,{m}_{2}=2,\\,{m}_{3}=3,\\,{m}_{4}=1.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $y$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}=3,\\,{y}_{2}=5,\\,{y}_{3}=2,\\,{y}_{4}=4.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3}+{m}_{4} \\\\  & =2+2+3+1 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{y}_{1}+{m}_{2}{y}_{2}+{m}_{3}{y}_{3}+{m}_{4}{y}_{4} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6+10+6+4 \\\\  & =26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{26}{8}=\\frac{13}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-163276/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163276"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163271/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer/id #uuid "777e4735-e2b2-5a93-bca2-73a2e03041cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163271/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "25d9595e-4c33-54ca-abe1-b7ff2be92f8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163271/selection/1512fbc4ba9ac54935748bd30a3df0f8adcca19968544e9199178dd45a802f05" :answer/id #uuid "1ecc71e3-cb63-53a7-8784-a1df56cc0fb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163271/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "d36e1303-030c-5c21-aa23-dd21041e849c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163271/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "7c02d07f-b9a2-590a-8636-7b4356f001f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163271/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e6b0750-2f04-5644-9b6b-9b8f19f207fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163271/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer-field/choices ["q-163271/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" "q-163271/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-163271/selection/1512fbc4ba9ac54935748bd30a3df0f8adcca19968544e9199178dd45a802f05" "q-163271/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-163271/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163271" :question/id #uuid "88a62ebc-9526-525a-badc-d55d33a5fa05" :question/math-academy-id "q-163271" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/fa8065896ec5efdc71402581c78674e4681fd02df2f7b945b0a182ae271fedfc.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above, where the distances along the $x$ and $y$ axes are measured in meters. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=6,\\,{m}_{2}=2,\\,{m}_{3}=4.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $x$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-3,\\,{x}_{2}=2,\\,{x}_{3}=4.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =6+2+4 \\\\  & =12\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =6\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-18+4+16 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{2}{12}=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163271/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163271"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163270/selection/7e978c54170214b26427b3c2b51ec4318a6f72efb4904214de6989347746ebe9" :answer/id #uuid "ef6e0af3-65aa-5b12-8f0a-c9f23f76d025" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163270/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "03218cf4-827b-5a1e-8e59-f4cbc40ed725" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163270/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "630cd070-7add-55d9-af46-e9c5f4373caa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163270/selection/edc901e84f0cdd5174afd49105ac3883566ea0e1e057217fb66083a56cc119ba" :answer/id #uuid "84b56a9e-ed15-509c-8d96-7d3d9d6cf663" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163270/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer/id #uuid "c09699a9-2daf-5420-813b-20f17608bcb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163270/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "051f6b2b-56fc-520f-80c0-7777ab3daa3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163270/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer-field/choices ["q-163270/selection/7e978c54170214b26427b3c2b51ec4318a6f72efb4904214de6989347746ebe9" "q-163270/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-163270/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-163270/selection/edc901e84f0cdd5174afd49105ac3883566ea0e1e057217fb66083a56cc119ba" "q-163270/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163270" :question/id #uuid "0982dd6f-cd45-5da5-a485-8151218b8587" :question/math-academy-id "q-163270" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/5d66682c96a14fb37ea0eb2deb46190fbe651e013a05c16a95577423b49b0ab9.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above, where the distances along the $x$ and $y$ axes are measured in meters. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=1,\\,{m}_{2}=3,\\,{m}_{3}=6.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $x$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-4,\\,{x}_{2}=-2,\\,{x}_{3}=3.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =1+3+6 \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-4)+3\\cdot (-2)+6\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-4-6+18 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{8}{10}=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163270/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163270"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163273/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" :answer/id #uuid "da2af8f1-6aec-59f9-9e7a-da7076fec528" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163273/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "94500576-b1f7-5216-8285-d5ecbd06af04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163273/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "5459ccf6-aecb-5f8f-812d-ddef748a11b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163273/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "aac7b468-bdbb-54a9-8d6a-658845cffdf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163273/selection/f7e51073a8044d706f62a310ce4d8f162b2fb8c60dce078b4b3b822d9f8ed6fa" :answer/id #uuid "337c413f-07ba-5a16-9706-d530e66a0550" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163273/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e3463db-8436-5774-9126-4622b4ecd0b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163273/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer-field/choices ["q-163273/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" "q-163273/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-163273/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-163273/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" "q-163273/selection/f7e51073a8044d706f62a310ce4d8f162b2fb8c60dce078b4b3b822d9f8ed6fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163273" :question/id #uuid "eedfc815-4546-56aa-9cb7-6ee7b9d4611a" :question/math-academy-id "q-163273" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/df6c2234a0b62d04157db126350e9b71f861af34ab42769245e553a8e228cb2b.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=2,\\,{m}_{2}=3,\\,{m}_{3}=1.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $y$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}=4,\\,{y}_{2}=2,\\,{y}_{3}=2.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =2+3+1 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{y}_{1}+{m}_{2}{y}_{2}+{m}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =8+6+2 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{16}{6}=\\frac{8}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-163273/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163273"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163269/selection/ed43d5224151224cedff9572a0bc31a320bd7a8ebd2aa526ca5884904c9d6cb4" :answer/id #uuid "905526be-2318-5e50-aa09-4b9997e4628d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163269/selection/bcbe057cec11b06e556ce6eb64efebcbc7b9b530f339b3d67669620f3e550dc2" :answer/id #uuid "c7678f6c-2b0e-5a68-81f8-0afaadbae74d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163269/selection/03807e04226c21d41cca4e8416f2bc03c1722f338720ca65704d3ea579b665a1" :answer/id #uuid "4d92d281-ccf7-5ff7-9616-05da58dad866" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163269/selection/29648ef4e020fc43d1b46acbdbbedfd18f3de75ade3ca2e0ef505839d2f8c39b" :answer/id #uuid "3b59f070-5553-5d4e-a069-9d1fb5eb7eb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163269/selection/f6c9d50fedf74e2b4ac0a2ef4f0295074416c004a23e123233fa99180084a57f" :answer/id #uuid "27ec6b6b-9a39-5437-9d6a-142b2539bb5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{23}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163269/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7589019-c054-5d94-8d8f-ad0b87c00c0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163269/selection/f6c9d50fedf74e2b4ac0a2ef4f0295074416c004a23e123233fa99180084a57f" :answer-field/choices ["q-163269/selection/ed43d5224151224cedff9572a0bc31a320bd7a8ebd2aa526ca5884904c9d6cb4" "q-163269/selection/bcbe057cec11b06e556ce6eb64efebcbc7b9b530f339b3d67669620f3e550dc2" "q-163269/selection/03807e04226c21d41cca4e8416f2bc03c1722f338720ca65704d3ea579b665a1" "q-163269/selection/29648ef4e020fc43d1b46acbdbbedfd18f3de75ade3ca2e0ef505839d2f8c39b" "q-163269/selection/f6c9d50fedf74e2b4ac0a2ef4f0295074416c004a23e123233fa99180084a57f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163269" :question/id #uuid "46ba6274-3fb3-5494-8cf2-40289eb1d004" :question/math-academy-id "q-163269" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/df939119a0cb5b9a5fdafc5158ecd299e91477247d7d6e920e2e167921ba4bdd.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above, where the distances along the $x$ and $y$ axes are measured in meters. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=2,\\,{m}_{2}=1,\\,{m}_{3}=7.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $x$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-3,\\,{x}_{2}=1,\\,{x}_{3}=4.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =2+1+7 \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot 1+7\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-6+1+28 \\\\  & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{23}{10}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163269/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163269"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12533"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/440f58e3d5e652374689083ffa672f505888259a51e1c5ef2207d94410eb8cab.png)\n\n     \n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $9\\,\\rm{ft}$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If $B$ has mass $10\\,\\rm{lb}$ and is $4\\,\\rm{ft}$ from the fulcrum, find the mass of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $m$ be the mass of $A.$\nThe length of the rod is $9\\,\\rm{ft}$ and the distance between the fulcrum and $B$ is $4\\,\\rm{ft}.$ So, the distance between the fulcrum and $A$ is\n\n$$\n9 - 4 = 5\\,\\rm{ft},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/dc2503e1ed1cd91a9f3876ec5735d5c375c36b9bcac6216659a29f5efa294ea0.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-m \\cdot 5 = -5m\\,\\textrm{lb}\\cdot\\textrm{ft}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $10 \\cdot 4 = 40\\,\\textrm{lb}\\cdot\\textrm{ft}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}40-5m & =0 \\\\ 5m & =40 \\\\ m & =8\\,lb.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12530"] :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses $m_1=1\\,\\textrm{kg},$ $m_2=2\\,\\textrm{kg},$ $m_3=3\\,\\textrm{kg},$ and $m_4=3\\,\\textrm{kg}$ located at $x_1=-1\\,\\textrm{m},$ $x_2 = 1\\,\\textrm{m},$ $x_3 = 3\\,\\textrm{m},$ and $x_4 = 5 \\, \\textrm{m},$ respectively, along the $x$-axis. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses $m_1,m_2,\\ldots,m_n$ located at $x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\nM_O = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i x_i.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =1, & \\,{m}_{2} & =2, & \\,{m}_{3} & =3, & \\,{m}_{4} & =3, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =1, & \\,{x}_{3} & =3, & \\,{x}_{4} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-1+2+9+15 \\\\  & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $25\\,\\textrm{kg} \\cdot \\textrm{m}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12531"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/cea41dc5efa961e4d0e3ccf42db21113d3b7d1d2240f3edbcc4c1f0cab61ead1.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overline{x},$ of a collection of point masses $m_1,m_2,\\ldots,m_n$ located at $x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{M_O}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n m_i$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_O = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i x_i$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =2, & \\,{m}_{2} & =4, & \\,{m}_{3} & =3, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =2, & \\,{x}_{3} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =2+4+3 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-2+8+12 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{M_O}{m} = \\dfrac{18}{9}=2.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12532"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/0e4802c6642fc0950358235f30fb8c994d26b912e557122af08b99277bb6192a.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overline{x}, \\overline{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overline{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses $m_1,m_2,\\ldots,m_n$ located at $(x_1y_1),(x_2,y_2),\\ldots,(x_n,y_n)$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overline{x},\\overline{y}) = \\left(\\dfrac{M_y}{m},\\dfrac{M_x}{m}\\right),\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n m_i$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_x = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i y_i$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_y = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i x_i$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\nm_1 = 3, \\qquad m_2 = 5, \\qquad m_3 = 1.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $y$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\ny_1 = 3, \\qquad y_2 = 0, \\qquad y_3 = 3.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =3+5+1 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{y}_{1}+{m}_{2}{y}_{2}+{m}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 3+5\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =9+0+3 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{M_x}{m} = \\dfrac{12}{9} = \\dfrac{4}{3}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
